### 5. `usePathUrlStrategy()` removed — hash-based URLs on web

**File:** `.agents/skills/flutter-setup-declarative-routing/SKILL.md` ~line 88

The new `main()` example:

```dart
void main() {
  runApp(const ProviderScope(child: MyApp()));
}
```

The prior version called `usePathUrlStrategy()` before `runApp()`. go_router 17.x does not internalize URL strategy; the Flutter engine defaults to `HashUrlStrategy`. Without the call, all web routes use `#`-fragment URLs (`https://example.com/#/settings`), breaking deep-links, bookmarks, and server-side routing. The project has a `web/` directory confirming web is a target.

**Fix:** Add `usePathUrlStrategy()` back before `runApp()` and re-add the import:

```dart
import 'package:flutter_web_plugins/url_strategy.dart';

void main() {
  usePathUrlStrategy();
  runApp(const ProviderScope(child: MyApp()));
}
```

